---
import FunnelLayout from '../../layouts/FunnelLayout.astro';
import { ROLE } from '../../data/household-role';
---

<FunnelLayout
  title="Your offer: household manager role"
  description="Offer details and everything needed before the first day."
  eyebrow="Step five · The offer"
  headline="We'd like you to <em>take the job</em>."
  lede="Here's the offer in full, and everything that needs to happen before your first real day. Nothing here should be a surprise, but read it properly and ask about anything that isn't clear."
>
  <div class="facts">
    <div class="fact"><dt>Role</dt><dd>{ROLE.title}, part-time</dd></div>
    <div class="fact"><dt>Rate</dt><dd>${ROLE.hourlyRate} per hour</dd></div>
    <div class="fact"><dt>Hours</dt><dd>About {ROLE.hoursPerWeek} per week</dd></div>
    <div class="fact"><dt>Schedule</dt><dd>[TODO: the days and times you agreed]</dd></div>
    <div class="fact"><dt>Typical week</dt><dd>About ${ROLE.weeklyPay} gross</dd></div>
    <div class="fact"><dt>Paid</dt><dd>Every two weeks by direct deposit, through {ROLE.payrollService}</dd></div>
    <div class="fact"><dt>Start date</dt><dd>[TODO: first real day]</dd></div>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong>This offer is conditional on a background check.</strong> That's the only condition,
      and it's standard. Step two below covers exactly what it involves and what your rights are.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What the job includes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>W-2 employment with taxes withheld, so this shows up as real earnings history for you</li>
    <li>Paid leave accruing under Illinois law, usable for any reason, no explanation needed</li>
    <li>Mileage on errands reimbursed at the IRS rate, and a household card so you never front money</li>
    <li>All supplies and equipment provided</li>
    <li>A written priority list, so you always know what matters most when time runs short</li>
    <li>A rate review at least once a year</li>
    <li>A check-in every two weeks for the first two months, then monthly</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Three things to do before your first day</h2>

  <h3>1. Read and sign the employment agreement</h3>
  <p>
    We'll send it separately. It covers the schedule, rate, duties, the priority order, time off,
    what happens when we travel, and notice periods on both sides. Read it properly. If anything
    in it doesn't match what we discussed, say so before you sign, not after.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Background check paperwork</h3>
  <p>
    Two short forms: a disclosure telling you we intend to run a check, and your authorization.
    We pay for it. If anything comes back that gives us pause, you get a copy of the full report
    and a real chance to respond before any decision is made. That's your right under federal law,
    and we'll follow it properly.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Payroll setup</h3>
  <p>
    {ROLE.payrollService} will email you directly to collect your W-4 and I-9 and set up direct
    deposit. For the I-9 you'll need to show original documents in person on or before your first
    day. A passport works alone, or a driver's license plus a Social Security card or birth
    certificate.
  </p>

  <h2>What we'll have ready for you</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      No key or code to keep track of. I work from home, so I'll be here to let you in. If we
      later find you'd rather have your own key, we'll sort that out then
    </li>
    <li>The household card for groceries and supplies</li>
    <li>A shared running list for "we're out of X" and one-off requests</li>
    <li>Written preferences on the handful of things we're genuinely particular about</li>
    <li>The written priority order, so the first week isn't guesswork</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Saying yes</h2>
  <p>
    Reply to our email or text <a href={ROLE.interviewPhoneHref} class="link-underline">{ROLE.interviewPhone}</a>. If you want a day or two to think it over,
    take it. If something in here needs adjusting, tell us now while it's easy to change.
  </p>
  <p>
    And if the answer is no, please just say so plainly. We'd much rather know.
  </p>
</FunnelLayout>
